            {
                "entry_id": "9b7704ba-8d5b-3e82-a145-1b3679ec2f24",
                "word": "acromion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b475e1f2-c919-4d7d-8266-9c49d85e2466",
                        "entry_id": "9b7704ba-8d5b-3e82-a145-1b3679ec2f24",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "acromions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                        "entry_id": "9b7704ba-8d5b-3e82-a145-1b3679ec2f24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Protubérance osseuse latérale partant de l’épine de l’omoplate (scapula) et qui va s'articuler avec la clavicule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3e61690-d8c9-4612-ba79-7954dd4e37b9",
                                "sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                                "text": "Le moyne avec son baston de croix luy donna entre col et collet sur l’os acromion si rudement qu’il l’estonna."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de18bc0b-affc-4726-815b-89f65b37c86d",
                                "sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                                "text": "— Alors, curé, tu n’y crois pas, à ces reliques ?\n— Non, pas aux leurs, je crois aux miennes. J’ai l’os acromion de sainte Diétrine, qui éclaircit l’urine et le teint des diétreux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6999122-22f5-440f-b9b0-aa52a8834a51",
                                "sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                                "text": "Un paparazzi mitraillait Amanda von Comodoro-Rivadavia qui fondait, ru lacrymal, sur l’acromion d’Urbain d’Agostino, son soupirant favori."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b77e8322-060c-4db3-9882-c1565f7c9120",
                                "sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                                "text": "...dans le miroir, chaque soir avant de se doucher, elle regardait ses os saillant sous la peau, les acromions qui faisaient deux petites crêtes en haut des épaules, la ligne tendue des clavicules, ce drôle de point au milieu du sternum."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07220feb-fc9c-4fe1-93d9-1874bc1f29fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b7704ba-8d5b-3e82-a145-1b3679ec2f24",
                        "source_sense_id": "71bd2cc2-3230-3bd2-a29d-3cba553f9d96",
                        "target_lang_word": "acromion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "acromion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                        "entry_id": "9347cb5d-7056-3e49-8694-465a00c52f80",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The outermost point of the shoulder blade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9563d01d-fe68-48d2-9a7f-fcbbce2cd20c",
                                                "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                                "text": "\"The ball struck the fore part of HIS LORDSHIP'S epaulette; and entered the left shoulder immediately before the processus acromion scapulae, which it slightly fractured."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1bcb9bb-a9de-4085-ac2e-c3d2beab01c0",
                                                "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                                "text": "The deltoid is wasted, and the acromion unduly prominent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a2f1973-1c7d-49eb-96f2-9d0332a4dd7c",
                                                "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                                "text": "Complete pectoral and pelvic bones show a deep subrectangular acromion on the scapula and a low obturator flange on the ischium."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d405f588-ab71-4262-8349-5456a7277ac2",
                                                "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                                "text": "The preserved portions of the scapula are sufficient to determine that the acromion projected well beyond the glenoid and that the axillary margin was longer than the vertebral."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5f570bd-2f34-4ab1-aec8-233d45be6ca1",
                                                "sense_id": "81952989-8ced-3b5e-8f34-93d8a45dfd10",
                                                "text": "The clavicle is a small flat bone like that of a dog (1), here preserved near the coracoid processes lying parallel to and slightly behind the acromion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b8e72e9e-3163-43b9-a371-475b3a488712",
